{title: 619 - Lead On, O King Eternal}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #619 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 619}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]Lead on, O [Dm/A]King [F]Eternal,
[C/G]The [F]day of [Em/B]march [Am]has [G]come;
[G7/F]Henceforth [A#dim]in [Dm/A]fields [F]of [Em]conquest
[Em/G]Thy [G]tents shall [F#m]be our [G]home.
[G7/F]Through [Em]days [A#dim]of [C7/A#]preparation
[G]Thy [F#m]grace [C]has [Dm]made [C]us [Bdim]strong;
[G/B]And [C]now, O [Am]King [C7/A#]eternal,
[F]We [Em]lift our [Dm/F]battle [C/E]song.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em]Lead on, O [Dm/A]King [F]eternal,
[C/G]till [F]sin's fierce [Em/B]war [Am]shall [G]cease,
[G7/F]and [Em]holiness [F]shall [Em]whisper
[Em/G]the [G]sweet amen [F#m/A]of [G]peace.
[G7/F]For [Em]not [A#dim]with [C7/A#]swords loud [Am]clashing,
[G]nor [F#m]roll [C]of [Dm]stirring [Bdim]drums;
[G/B]with [C]deeds of [Am]love [C7/A#]and [C]mercy
[F]the heavenly [Dm/F]kingdom [G/D]comes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Em]Lead on, O [Dm/A]King [F]eternal,
[C/G]we [F]follow, [Em/B]not [Am]with [G]fears,
[G7/F]for [Em]gladness [Dm/A]breaks [F]like [Em]morning
[Em/G]where'er [G]thy [F#m]face appears.
[G7/F]Thy [Em]cross [A#dim]is [C7/A#]lifted [Am]o'er us,
[G]we [F#m]journey [Dm]in [C]its [Bdim]light;
[G/B]the [C]crown awaits [C7/A#]the [C]conquest;
[F]lead [Em]on, O [Dm/F]God [G/D]of [C/E]might.
{end_of_verse}
